  <static seed="27" source="Contrib/CCCS/QuantitativeLiteracy/IA_6.1/OpenStax_IA_6.1_53.pg">
    <statement><p>Factor the given polynomial</p>
<p><m>{3t^{3}-24t^{2}+12t-96}=</m> <fillin characters="19" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>If the expression cannot be factored then answer with <alert>prime</alert>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3\mathopen{}\left(t^{2}+4\right)\mathopen{}\left(t-8\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>There is a greatest common factor of <m>3</m>.  Start by factoring that out.</p>
<p><m>3({t^{3}-8t^{2}+4t-32})</m></p>
<p>Then we can factor the remaining expression by grouping.</p>
<p><m>3(t^2(t - 8) + 4(t - 8))</m></p>
<p><m>{3\mathopen{}\left(t^{2}+4\right)\mathopen{}\left(t-8\right)}</m></p>
</solution>
